F('T05', 'telemetry', 'measured', 'The arms never ran equal software. Run 1: AMD ran vLLM 0.27.1.dev5 (image rocm/vllm, tuned MI300X MoE config) against CUDA vLLM 0.30.0 (default FP8 MoE config); Run 2 and 3 AMD ran vLLM 0.30.0 in a different image. Run 3 has the same vLLM version on both vendors but different kernels selected: AITER FP8 MoE and AiterFp8BlockScaled GEMM on AMD; Triton FP8 MoE, FlashInfer/DeepGEMM FP8 GEMM and FLASH_ATTN on the H100.',
  {'run1': {'amd': {'vllm': '0.27.1.dev5+gf46a9dfe2.d20260827.rocm100', 'image': 'rocm/vllm@sha256:30761c2125ce150d556bef46406a0158446421886bf83a2e60154c6e4ca17a13', 'rocm': '7.2.4'}, 'nvidia': {'vllm': '0.30.0', 'image': 'vllm/vllm-openai@sha256:8a69ffad015f138d7170c4ddc429e230a3bc1c1719f67e14324749df200a4b90', 'driver': '580.173.02'}},
            'run2_run3_amd': {'vllm': '0.30.0', 'image': 'vllm/vllm-openai-rocm@sha256:2e7da1ad1c66836802072588adea75f9f4991da5f9545b4318e91d422c22ce6a', 'rocm': '7.2.3'},
            'run3_selected_kernels': {'A/T0': ['ROCM_ATTN (auto, TURBOQUANT overridden)', 'AiterFp8BlockScaledMMKernel', 'AITER Fp8 MoE backend'], 'A/T1': ['ROCM_AITER_FA (forced)', 'AiterFp8BlockScaledMMKernel', 'AITER Fp8 MoE backend'], 'N/T0': ['FLASH_ATTN', 'FlashInferFp8DeepGEMMDynamicBlockScaledKernel', 'TRITON Fp8 MoE backend', 'FlashInfer top-p/top-k sampling']},
            'run2_fp8_linear_kernel': 'RowWiseTorchFP8ScaledMMLinearKernel (torch fallback) on AMD in both auto and forced arms',
            'run1_serve_log_collected': False, 'run3_kv_cache_tokens': {'A/T0': 1484848, 'A/T1': 1484960, 'N/T0': 430592}},
  ev(R+'hotaisle-mi300x/env.normalized.json', R+'do-h100/env.normalized.json', R+'run2-hotaisle-mi300x/env.json', R+'run3-scored-a-t0/serve.log', R+'run3-scored-a-t1/serve.log', R+'run3-scored-n-t0/serve.log', R+'run3-scored-a-t0/invocation.json', C+'DISCLOSURES.md'),
  'ours', 'Run 1 kernel identity comes from DISCLOSURES (observed live, serve logs not collected); Run 2/3 kernel identity is read from serve.log selection lines. The Run 3 comparison is a different-complete-configuration comparison (MANUAL.md label), so it prices a stack, not a chip.', 'When a price gap is quoted between two vendors, name the kernels each stack selected; a stack change can move the answer as much as the price does (Run 2: attention backend alone moved throughput up to 46%).', 'high (serve.log selection lines)', 'Run each vendor with its best tuned kernels in a frozen tier design (T0 auto / T1 tuned) on both sides, as the Run 3 PREREG intended for AMD only.', 'Run 1 2026-09-23; Run 2 2026-09-23; Run 3 2026-09-24')
